' Question: what happens to a Spot Grid whose price feed goes quiet and comes back?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md (Planned, EPIC-042C). Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-halt-recovery
participant "Price watch\n(5 s beat)" as W
participant "BotRunState" as S
participant "HaltRecoveryDirector" as D
participant "GridExecutor\n(bot's worker)" as G
participant "GridResumeSequence" as R
participant trading as T
participant alerting as A

W -> S : no tick for 60 s: halt(price_feed_stale)
S -> D : which event? (state, policy, ledger)
D --> S : halt_transient (budget left)
S -> S : RUNNING --halt_transient--> AWAITING_RECOVERY\nladder taken off, base kept, exits still watched
loop every beat while AWAITING_RECOVERY
  W -> G : is price_feed_stale clear? (probe)
  G -> G : clear since = first clear sample;\na not-clear sample resets it
end
G -> G : clear for 120 s: save the attempt in the bot record
G -> T : fresh price: beyond the stop loss or take profit?
alt crossed
  G -> G : Stop, sell base forced; no ladder is laid
else not crossed
  G -> R : propose(price)  (budget, cancel tagged, new plan)
  R -> T : cancel tagged orders, read inventory
  G -> R : confirm(proposal, condition_cleared)
  R -> T : lay the ladder
  R -> S : AWAITING_RECOVERY --condition_cleared--> STARTING --> RUNNING
  G -> A : BotAutoRecoveredEvent
end
note over G, D : a refused attempt keeps the bot waiting and spends the attempt;\nbudget spent, wait limit passed or a restart: HALTED
@enduml
